    "pejero": {
      "form": "pejerō",
      "claim": "no macron before j",
      "against": "Lewis &amp; Short <span lang=\"la\">pējĕro</span>; Traupman 196 <span lang=\"la\">pēierāre</span>",
      "html": "House orthography: the vowel before an intervocalic j takes no macron, the syllable being heavy by the double j (<span lang=\"la\">pejor, ejus</span>). The word is <span lang=\"la\">perjūrō</span> reshaped (Lewis &amp; Short), not a compound with a long prefix such as <span lang=\"la\">dē-</span> or <span lang=\"la\">prō-</span>, which would keep its macron.",
